# Hermes Mobile

<!-- impeccable:product-schema 1 -->

## Platform

android

## Stack

Native Android views, with Java and the Android SDK (API 28–36, zero WebView, minimal dependencies: Firebase Messaging and UnifiedPush Connector). This app requires our Hermes Agent fork at [{{ fork_repository }}]({{ fork_url }}) for single-host multi-profile `/p/{profile}`, run-scoped instructions, Live UI modding (`ui.patch`), universal push deliveries (`mobile_deliver`), universal same-server sharing, Smart Notes, pattern-gated habits, visual approval diffs, Brain Studio, and the approved device bridge.

## Users and operating context

People use their own protected Hermes profile to chat, write code, manage personal knowledge, and return to long-running work from a phone or tablet in English or French. **One single HTTPS server hostname** serves all users and profiles under `/p/<profile>`, each isolated in its own profile directory with its own private workspace, provider credentials, and 256-bit access key—without needing a separate HTTPS hostname per person. A device can hold more than one account, and users on the same server can share notes, skills, surfaces, widgets, tools, artifacts, and discussions with one another.

## Product purpose

Resume a conversation, see what happened while away, and act on the work in the same thread. Coding sessions need readable syntax-highlighted code and visual hunk diffs, visible tool activity, and explicit approval requests. Artifacts and pinned tools belong to their originating conversation.

People describe what they want in everyday language, by typing, dictating, or using hands-free Duplex Voice. Hermes can ask follow-up questions, propose interactive tools or live screen adaptations, suggest habits after observing repeated patterns (`>= 3` occurrences), and prepare native Android actions for review before opening another app.

## Capabilities and constraints

- **Four adaptive workspaces.** **Discussions**, **Workspace**, **Brain**, and **Activity** adapt automatically between an IME-aware phone bottom bar and a 92 dp tablet navigation rail with a dual-pane conversation sidebar.
- **Quick command palette & reusable workflows.** A 1-tap searchable overlay (`Ctrl+K` / `Cmd+K`) jumps across actions, recent threads, and encrypted per-profile templates while strictly preserving the Editable Draft Rule.
- **Concurrent multi-run & multi-user isolation.** Run multiple simultaneous tasks across different discussions for one unlocked profile without canceling active streams or mixing updates, alongside persisted passphrase backoff and atomic profile deletion.
- **Live Connection Doctor.** Parallel non-blocking checks verify server latency, companion fork capabilities (`51/51`), push, updates, ambient permissions, and language sync with 1-tap fixes and a strictly redacted safe report.
- **Single source of truth & transparency.** Sessions, jobs, model inventory, capabilities, and available tools come from the connected fork runtime. Usage metrics show their source and scope; unavailable measurements remain visibly unknown rather than fabricated zeros.
- **Zero-leak private alerts & deliveries.** Closed-app alerts (FCM or self-hosted UnifiedPush) carry only opaque routing metadata. Titles, messages, and delivery payloads stay on the authenticated gateway until the user unlocks the owning profile.
- **Fail-closed privacy by default.** Local credentials and drafts are encrypted per profile with optional Class-3 biometric unlock and configurable lock grace. Ambient Intelligence (notifications, media, calendar, contacts) starts completely OFF per profile and hard-blocks OTP/2FA codes, password managers, banking apps, and secret lockscreen notifications before content enters memory.
- **Observable, reversible customization.** Live UI patches (`ui.patch`), Surfaces v2, WCAG-AA theme overrides, and profile-scoped Home Screen Widgets require explicit preview/confirmation and retain full rollback history.

## Product principles

- Keep the transcript and composer within reach during ongoing work across phones, tablets, rotation, and split-screen windows.
- Keep each question and its answer together. A tap on an approval applies only to the exact request it names.
- Let people edit a dictated message before sending it, and keep the keyboard available whenever voice input is unavailable.
- Preserve the user's place, drafts, and selections across disconnects, window resizes, incoming events, and account switches.
- Keep both the French and English interfaces free of unnecessary technical jargon and fully usable with the keyboard visible, TalkBack, 150% text scale, and light or dark appearance, following the Impeccable Design System Single Source of Truth in [`.impeccable/design.json`](.impeccable/design.json) and [`DESIGN.md`](DESIGN.md) (*"A paper workspace for conversation"*).
- Make changes to tools, providers, reminders, widgets, and screen layouts explicit, bounded, and reversible.
